                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "Drag a chip; a 4px accent bar on a neighbour\u2019s leading or trailing edge marks where it lands. No slot opens between chips \u2014 a finger-wide gap has to come out of the run, which relays the whole strip the instant a press matures: chips sliding, rows appearing and disappearing, and on a scrolled 1024\u00d7600 console the panel shortening, the scroll clamping, and the run sliding out from under the finger. Each chip\u2019s two halves are the drop targets instead \u2014 a far bigger target than any gap between chips could be. The add chip stays in place during a drag and only goes dark: removing it could empty a row and shorten the panel the same way."
              }
            ],
            "textTransform": "none",
